Verified with vitest unit tests (bridge + projection) and one integration test hitting the real route with a merged legacy fixture.

**Test suite** (12 total: 7 new, 5 existing regression):

```ts
describe("LegacyBridge → ROLES_ASSIGNED", () => {
  it("emits one synthetic ROLES_ASSIGNED at game end with full roster", () => {
    const bridge = new LegacyBridge(bus, store);
    bus.emit("game.end", legacyEnd({ players: [
      { id: "p1", role: "WEREWOLF" },
      { id: "p2", persona: { gameRole: "SEER" } },   // no p.role
      { id: "p3" },                                   // plain villager
    ]}));
    expect(store.appended).toHaveLength(1);
    expect(store.appended[0].roster).toEqual([
      { playerId: "p1", role: "WEREWOLF" },
      { playerId: "p2", role: "SEER" },
      { playerId: "p3", role: "VILLAGER" },           // persona fallback
    ]);
  });

  it("dedupes replays — game.end fired twice appends once", () => { /* dedupeKey */ });

  it("player with no role info degrades to UNASSIGNED, never crashes", () => {
    expect(applyRolesAssigned(emptyState, evt).players[0].role).toBe("UNASSIGNED");
  });
});

describe("projection: first-write-wins", () => {
  it("fills only UNASSIGNED gaps; existing roles are never overwritten", () => { /* ... */ });
  it("ignores roster entries for players not in the game", () => { /* ... */ });
});

describe("GET /api/v1/games/:id?limit", () => {
  it("slices AFTER merging legacy rows — merged overflow no longer exceeds limit", () => { /* ... */ });
  it("limit=undefined returns all rows; limit>total returns all", () => { /* ... */ });
});
```

**Results:**

| Case | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| Legacy game, no modern event | villagers `UNASSIGNED` (heuristic only) | full roster from `p.role || p.persona.gameRole` |
| Plain villager (`p.role` absent, persona `VILLAGER`) | `UNASSIGNED` | `VILLAGER` |
| Existing `ROLES_ASSIGNED` + synthetic end event | — | prior roles kept; only gaps filled |
| Duplicate `game.end` / replay | double-write risk | one event (dedupeKey) |
| `?limit=5` with 3 DB + 4 legacy rows | returned 5 DB rows + 4 legacy = 9 (overflow) | merged → sliced → exactly 5 |
| No `?limit` / `limit` ≥ total | n/a | full merged list |
| Docs commands | `tsx --` (not runnable via `npm run`) | `dev --` runs; routes match route table |

**Edge cases covered:** player present in event but absent from game (ignored), missing `persona`, `endedAt` absent (falls back to `timestamp`), legacy event arriving after a modern roster (no overwrite), and merged rows with duplicate event IDs (deduped before slicing).

